wn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408)\nr3 rework against reviewer verdict 02 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1). The finding was independently re-verified before acceptance and CONFIRMED three ways: .spec/platform-distribution.md:103-105 mandates the Sparkle -spks/-spki Mach lookup exceptions for the sandboxed host; this repo own .research/260721_macos-self-update.md:111-113 records the identical two-value set; and codesign -d --entitlements :- across /Applications found six shipping apps carrying exactly that pattern, three of them sandboxed with those two values and nothing else. Fix: macos.host now authors com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name as required-adjacent with the exact authored array plus a resolvedValue for bundle-level checking, portalCapability false, owner uyju7n, project-architecture attribution (attributionNote states why it is not sandbox-consequence, unlike network.client). Rule X1 added because the same spec clause bans unreviewed exception entitlements: a reviewed-exception register plus a banned set for Hardened Runtime relaxations, with get-task-allow deliberately left to A10d. Assertions A10e, A14, A15 added; R27 pins the assertion id set so it cannot silently shrink again. Two evidence notes recorded rather than smoothed over: Tailscale ships the exception while unsandboxed (so shipping-product presence is not proof of requirement), and Sparkle binary names three endpoint suffixes (-spks, -spki, -spkp) of which only two are entitled, making the two-value set deliberate. Gates: reviewer own targeted jq gate now true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1);