 exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. All three harnesses re-verified running in place from the board resource layout; every command run without a pipeline because zsh carries no PIPESTATUS. One board field changed on one element: TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope, revision label r7 -> r8, character delta 0, verified byte-exact. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-linked; no portal mutation; no product source, spec file or generated project touched. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-75338f, pid=79427, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-ae0e2a, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-ae0e2a)\nr9 self-audit after the r8 handoff. THERE IS NO VERDICT 08 - this revision was not requested by a reviewer; it reports what the audit found. r8 was re-run untouched first and was intact (1331 checks, 164/164 negative gates, 44 board checks, all exit 0), so nothing here repairs drift that had already appeared. Two defect classes found and closed. RULE D1: the matrix has carried a prose consumers list since r1 and it was never compared against the board dependency graph. Transitive closure over every task and bug record: 19 declared consumers, 16 reachable, 3 NOT - TASK-260715-1o9wjz, TASK-260715-3f4lxy and TASK-260715-29ws8l had no dependency path to this task at all, so a max_parallel=1 scheduler could have run the macOS credential resolver, the snapshot loader and the profile-trust contract