un completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c, pid=26992, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f)\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-6ab34f, pid=34042, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4)\nReviewer verdict 09 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, route analysis. Blocking F1: r10 pre-authorizes conditional exception X1-C1, but R39 accepts coordinated drift of its exact least-privilege path, signing-channel set, and arming owner. Independent mutations widened /Library/Keychains/ to /, removed developer-id from channelsIfArmed, and changed armedBy from TASK-260715-1uxx3i to TASK-260715-9yp8to; validate-matrix.py exited 0 for all three when each negative control must exit 1. Supplied gates remain green: validator 2654 exit 0, mutations 220/220 exit 0, board A1/P1/D1 exit 0, both preservation gates exit 0, reviewer gates exit 0, legacy exit 0, board validate exit 0, swift test 335/29 exit 0. Full evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-09.md.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-83c1b4, pid=49397, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-17c375, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-17c375)\nr11 rework against reviewer verdict 09 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1 plus required rework items 2-5). F1 was reproduced before it was accepted, against the UNMODIFIED r10 artifact and with the r10 validator and r10 rationale, because judging r10 data with the r11 gate proves nothing: all three coordinated-drift mutations exited 0 where a negative control must exit 1. CONFIRMED. No entitlement decision, identifier, target row, profile row, record, assertion, assertion scope, open constraint or Ceremony C1 mutation set changed, and X1-C1 itself is byte-for-byte what r10 reviewed - r11 changes how it is CHECKED. Rule X1 gains conditionalExceptionDerivation and R39 now DERIVES every field instead of comparing the register to its own mirror on the row: target from the unique row carrying the K3 version scope, key from K3's arming instruction, value set from a path-subtree bound that no coordinated edit can widen, channel set from the target's own channels in full, arming owner from K3's resolutionOwner cross-checked against the rule-D1 consumer list, review revision from the revision log, scope sentence as a rendered clause. The reviewed path and the bound vocabulary live in the gate, because a bound that lives only inside the data it bounds is not a bound. The item-3 sweep found two