: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-c1a5a8, pid=73457, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1e0752, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1e0752)\nr12 rework against reviewer verdict 10 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1). The finding was independently reproduced against the unmodified r11 artifact before acceptance and CONFIRMED: X1-C1.reviewedIn moved from 2026-07-28.r10 to 2026-07-28.r2, validate-matrix.py PASS over 2805 checks, exit 0, where a negative control must exit 1. r11 had already documented this gap under a Stated bound heading in section 4.5 and gated it at membership anyway - writing a gap down is not closing it, which is why the fix is a derivation and not a stricter string. New rule X1-P (exceptionReviewProvenance) derives the revision each register entry first entered this contract in, from evidence older than the claim: snapshot-proven, from the digest-pinned per-revision baselines the preservation harnesses already consume (X1-C1 absent from r8 and r9, present in r10), and summary-attested as a fallback for an entry older than the oldest baseline (X1-A1 attested by r3), refused wherever the chain can decide; both cross-checked against the new revisionLog[].introduces record. The chain is protected against narrowing as well as tampering - contiguous to supersedes, no undeclared baseline left on disk - because dropping the snapshot in which an entry is absent silently demotes it to attestation. known-revision is REMOVED from the implemented bound