        "id": "A16",
        "text": "LEAST PRIVILEGE (rule G4) — com.apple.security.application-groups is ABSENT from every macOS bundle on every channel, production and probe alike, and no macOS provisioning profile's Entitlements dict carries the key or names an App Group. A macOS bundle or profile that carries it is a portal or build-setting drift finding for TASK-260715-3jloqy or TASK-260715-uyju7n, never a local exception"
      },
      {
        "id": "A17",
        "text": "LEAST PRIVILEGE (rule K2) — keychain-access-groups is ABSENT from every macOS bundle on every channel, production and probe alike. The macOS host reads and writes its own Data Protection Keychain items through its default access group 262RZ595FP.works.relux.tunnel.mac, which the injected com.apple.application-identifier entitlement provides, so a macOS bundle declaring keychain-access-groups is a build-setting drift finding for TASK-260715-uyju7n or a portal finding for TASK-260715-3jloqy, never a local exception. Asserted against the signed BUNDLE only: a Mac Development profile's team-wide keychain-access-groups = ['<TEAMID>.*'] wildcard is a profile property and is not a finding"
      },
      {
        "id": "A18",
        "text": "LEAST PRIVILEGE (rule G4) — com.apple.security.application-groups is ABSENT from both iOS probe bundles and no probe profile names an App Group. The iOS probe's host-to-provider exchange is NETunnelProviderSession.sendProviderMessage (TASK-260715-1jckn0 AC3), which needs no group; the probe App Group record was deleted in r5. This is the negative half of that task's AC5 archive inspection"
      },
      {
        "id": "A6",
        "text": "keychain-access-groups present only where status == required, which after r5 is ios.host and ios.provider alone; ABSENT from every macOS target, production and probe alike, and from the iOS probe pair. r5, rule K2: macos.host lost the group because no second macOS target reads it, so a macOS bundle carrying the key is drift for TASK-260715-uyju7n or TASK-260715-3jloqy, never a local exception"
      },
