        "id": "A19",
        "text": "CONDITIONAL FLOOR EXCEPTION (rule K3) - com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write is ABSENT from all eight signed bundles on every channel while register entry X1-C1 is unarmed. On macOS 26.5 (25F71) the base App Sandbox profile already grants the provider read and write access to /Library/Keychains, so authoring the exception there would be a least-privilege regression. That grant is an OS-version-scoped fact and is UNVERIFIED on the binding macOS 15.0 deployment floor. While the entry is unarmed, the key's presence in any bundle is a build-setting drift finding for TASK-260715-uyju7n. If TASK-260715-1uxx3i shows the grant is absent on the oldest supported macOS, the entry is armed under rule K3, the key becomes expected on macos.provider rather than drift, and it is still not a portal capability and still no change to the Ceremony C1 authorization scope."
