 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2335 — Four macOS Network Extensions development profiles provisioned (TASK-260715-3jloqy)
+- PORTAL RESULT: Xcode automatic provisioning created or updated exactly the four r12 macOS identifiers and downloaded one device-bound Mac Team Provisioning Profile for each: `works.relux.tunnel.mac`, `.mac.tunnel`, `.probe.mac`, and `.probe.mac.tunnel`. Network Extensions is profile-authorized on hosts and providers alike; no portal reauthentication or two-factor challenge occurred.
+- VALIDATION: All four profiles have team/prefix `262RZ595FP`, the exact application identifier, platform `OSX`, only the current Mac (`sha256:8ea3983a9990`), current validity through 2027-08-10, and unsuffixed `packet-tunnel-provider` without the Developer ID suffix. `com.apple.security.application-groups` is absent. The profile-only `keychain-access-groups = [262RZ595FP.*]` wildcard is expected under rule K2 and is not a finding.
+- SCOPE EVIDENCE: Exactly four local provisioning profiles changed during the run and all four are the approved macOS development set; no unexpected, iOS, or distribution profile changed. The isolated harness declared no App Group, Keychain Sharing, iOS, distribution, or legacy-bundle mutation, and raw profiles/certificates were neither attached nor committed.
+- ANOMALY: The portal/profile phase succeeded, but final local codesigning returned `errSecInternalComponent` for each harness target because unattended signing-key access was unavailable. A separate all-target no-sign compile succeeded. Read-only Safari automation also remained unavailable (timeout exit 142), consistent with APC34W-B5; neither issue caused a portal reauthentication challenge or invalidated the downloaded profiles.
+
 ### 2314 — Gate P0 Apple-account audit separates portal access from organization eligibility (TASK-260715-apc34w)
 - TECHNICAL EVIDENCE: Ceremony C1 records an authenticated Relux Works, LLC portal/team session and authority for matrix `2026-07-28.r12`. A team-scoped Xcode capability bundle refreshed on 2026-08-10 reports Network Extensions as public and editable for development and Developer ID distribution; local signing inventory includes the Relux Works Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities.
 - READINESS GAPS: The audit could not independently retrieve the Apple Developer membership enrollment type, active paid-through date, current Apple Developer Program License Agreement status, the operator's exact Account Holder/Admin role plus Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles grant, or a portal record proving that the current Apple-silicon Mac is registered. The Relux Works Account Holder owns membership/agreement proof; the Apple Platform/CI Admin and `TASK-260715-3jloqy` own role confirmation and Mac registration/profile evidence.

